<spell-notebook "tree-diagram theming">
	<header level="1">
		Tree diagram
		<header>A tree diagram draws a tree top-down:  a box for each node, a line to each of its children.</>
	</>
	<tree-diagram-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-tree-diagram-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root`
			for every diagram), or on one piece through `::part()`: `diagram` (the `<svg>`), `node` (each node),
			`root-node` (the root, also a `node`), `edge` (each line) and `slot-label`. Never set the
			`--_ui-tree-diagram-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.

			Colours default to Spell UI's own tokens (the root in `primary`, the other boxes on the muted
			surface), so a diagram follows the light or dark scheme by itself. Text sizes are the layout's: change
			them all at once with `--ui-tree-diagram-font-size`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every diagram on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-tree-diagram-edge-color: var(--ui-grey);
			  --ui-tree-diagram-min-scale: 0.6;
			}
			/* one diagram's root, in another colour */
			ui-tree-diagram.highlighted::part(root-node) {
			  --ui-tree-diagram-root-background: var(--ui-green-background);
			  --ui-tree-diagram-root-border-color: var(--ui-green);
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-tree-diagram" playground>
				<ui-tree-diagram>
					<script type="application/json">
						{
						  "label": "If",
						  "title": "if number / 15 is an integer",
						  "children": [
						    {
						      "label": "IsA · integer",
						      "detail": "boolean",
						      "slot": "condition",
						      "children": [
						        {
						          "label": "Divide",
						          "detail": "number",
						          "slot": "value",
						          "children": [
						            { "label": "Variable number", "detail": "number" },
						            { "label": "Number 15", "detail": "number" }
						          ]
						        }
						      ]
						    },
						    {
						      "label": "Print",
						      "slot": "body",
						      "children": [
						        { "label": "Variable number", "detail": "number" },
						        { "label": "Text \"fizzbuzz\"", "detail": "text" }
						      ]
						    },
						    { "label": "If …", "slot": "otherwise" }
						  ]
						}
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			A tree diagram is ours, not Fomantic's:  the theme menu in the header changes the page around it,
			and the colours it takes from Spell UI's tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
